  "limitations": [
    "Buffered within-state sampled-geography validation is not new-region or future-time validation.",
    "10 km blocks and 2 km buffers are fixed protocol choices, not proven independence ranges.",
    "Road-survey bias, pseudo-absence sampling and positional uncertainty remain.",
    "Spatial/control memberships and retained training sizes differ; their gap does not isolate a causal buffer effect.",
    "Five-fold sample SD is not a confidence interval or a significance test; training sets overlap.",
    "SVM margins are evaluated within folds; cross-fold margins are not pooled into a ranking metric.",
    "Classification uses training-only fold thresholds; it is not directly comparable with legacy threshold 0.5 or retrospective test-selected Youden.",
    "Scores are uncalibrated and cannot establish real-world landslide occurrence probabilities.",
    "Fold models are validation artifacts and do not replace deployed models or explain the preserved legacy RF SHAP figures.",
    "Training used resource-only portable wrappers with lower startup admission; scientific code/configuration were unchanged.",
    "Fit counts refer to completed planned jobs, excluding separate pilots and retained interrupted-attempt evidence."
  ]
